# Settings > Backups: the radios whose settings are on the card, one radio's backups, one
# backup, and that backup compared with the radio on the link.
#
# Three radios, because each says something the others cannot: the demo radio is connected and
# so offers "save" and "compare"; "Ridge" is the same device before it was switched to MeshCore,
# listed under the demo radio as well as on its own row; and the third is not here, so its
# backups can be read but not compared.
scene demo
clock 2026-09-29 14:20
delay 160
config
backups list

# Backups is two rows above About, which is the last; Profiles is between them.
tab settings
key down 24
key up 2
key a
hold 2200

# The connected radio's backups: its own three, and the one from before the switch.
key down
key a
hold 2400

# The newest backup: every fact its header holds, and at the bottom what can be done with it.
key down
key a
hold 2400
key down 40
hold 1600
key up 2
hold 1400

# Compared with the radio. The first frame says it is reading the radio, which is what the app
# is doing until it answers; then what differs, the backup's value first.
key a
hold 900
backups compare
hold 3400

# Put back: the sheet first, then the restore in flight, then the radio read again and matching.
key down
hold 900
key a
hold 2800
key up
key a
backups restoring
hold 2200
backups same
hold 2200

# Back out, each level landing on the row it was opened from.
key b
hold 900
key b
hold 900
key b
hold 1400
